    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #353\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed to branch `bb/relay-143-auth-v1-08-08-protect-every-existing-r-thr_iex8t73668`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #143: every existing route now sits behind the shared session-auth middleware (`authenticateRequest`, from issue #140), with a single documented list of the exceptions that stay public.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `aiUsageHandler.ts`, `approvalRequestsHandler.ts`, `agentRunHandler.ts`, `mcpAgentPageHandler.ts`: replaced the stopgap `SEMPREC_API_TOKEN` shared-secret check with `authenticateRequest(pool, req)`, called as the first step inside each handler's existing try/catch (which already mapped `UnauthorizedError` to a 401).\n- `serve.ts`: no longer requires `SEMPREC_API_TOKEN` at startup — that mechanism is fully retired.\n- `app.ts` (new): extracted `createDispatcher(pool, options)` from `serve.ts` so the full route wiring can be exercised in tests without a real process.\n- `routeMatrix.ts` (new): the single documented artifact of every HTTP route this service answers, tagged `public`/protected, with a `publicReason` required for each public one — currently: login, password-reset request/consume (#142), and `/api/setup` (#233/#234). Its header comment also records the investigation findings for the other surfaces the issue asked about: no WS-upgrade route is live anywhere in the repo, module routes are in-process only, the web client has no router/login page yet (so no view-path guard applies beyond the already-public setup wizard), and no health-probe endpoints exist.\n- `__tests__/routeMatrix.test.ts` (new): boots the real dispatcher and, for every `ROUTE_MATRIX` entry, asserts unauthenticated requests get 401 unless marked public — this is the route-matrix test the issue's acceptance criteria require.\n- Rewrote the 4 affected handler test files to authenticate via real login sessions instead of the old shared-secret token.\n- Removed the now-dead `SEMPREC_API_TOKEN` proxy wiring from `web/vite.config.ts` and updated a stale comment referencing it in `web/src/api/setupOperations.ts`.\n\n**Verification:** backend unit (114), integration (756, including the new route-matrix and rewritten auth tests), and e2e (5) tiers all pass; backend build, lint, and module-boundary check are clean; web typecheck, test suite (139), and lint are clean.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
